# MoonLight build-time options.
#
# These exist so the IDF Component Manager's dependency `rules` (in
# main/idf_component.yml) can branch on them: a rule's `if:` clause can test a
# Kconfig symbol, but only one that is *declared* (an undeclared symbol raises
# MissingKconfigError and fails the solve), so a plain sdkconfig.defaults line is
# not enough: the option must be declared here too.

menu "MoonLight"

    config MM_P4_WIFI
        bool "ESP32-P4: include WiFi via the on-board ESP32-C6 (esp_hosted)"
        default n
        help
            Pulls the esp_wifi_remote + esp_hosted managed components, which
            present the P4's companion ESP32-C6 radio through the standard
            esp_wifi_* API over SDIO. The P4 has no native radio.

            Set by both P4 builds (esp32p4rev1, esp32p4rev3) through
            sdkconfig.defaults.esp32p4-wifi. esp_hosted self-initializes at boot;
            a board lacking a C6 switches the radio off on its WiFi card, which
            keeps the network cascade off WiFi.

    config MM_HLS
        bool "HLS streaming via the hardware H.264 encoder (ESP32-P4 only)"
        # Constrain the VALUE, not the visibility. `depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4` would hide the
        # symbol on every other target, and idf_component.yml gates the esp_h264 dependency on
        # $CONFIG{MM_HLS}: the solver cannot read a symbol that is not visible, so every non-P4
        # build failed with "MM_HLS ... not found in any Kconfig file". A range-style guard keeps
        # the symbol readable everywhere while making y impossible off the P4.
        default y if IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4
        default n
        help
            Pulls the esp_h264 managed component and compiles the platform HLS
            encoder (hardware H.264 + MPEG-TS muxer + PSRAM segment ring) behind
            the same HlsDriver the host uses. Only the P4 has the encoder
            silicon; other chips keep this off and build nothing.

    config MM_USB_MIDI_HOST
        bool "USB MIDI host on the chip's own USB port"
        default y if IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3 && !MM_LITE
        default n
        help
            Pulls the espressif/usb managed component and compiles the USB MIDI
            host, so a class-compliant MIDI desk plugged into the board drives the
            MIDI service with no computer. On for every S3 firmware outside the
            4 MB tier (MM_LITE).

    config MM_HDMI
        bool "HDMI out through an LT8912B MIPI-DSI bridge (ESP32-P4 only)"
        # Constrain the VALUE, not the visibility, for the reason MM_HLS gives above: idf_component.yml
        # gates esp_lcd_lt8912b on $CONFIG{MM_HDMI}, which the solver cannot read when hidden.
        default y if IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4
        default n
        help
            Pulls Espressif's esp_lcd_lt8912b component and compiles the HDMI output:
            the MIPI-DSI bus, the LT8912B bridge on the board's I2C bus, and a PPA
            scale into the DPI framebuffer, behind HdmiDriver. Only the P4 has a
            MIPI-DSI controller; other chips keep this off and build nothing.

    config MM_USB_VIDEO
        bool "USB video capture from a UVC grabber (ESP32-P4 only)"
        # Constrain the VALUE, not the visibility, for the reason MM_HLS gives above: a `depends on`
        # hides the symbol, and idf_component.yml gates usb_host_uvc on $CONFIG{MM_USB_VIDEO}, which
        # the solver cannot read when hidden. hasUsbVideo requires the P4 too, so y elsewhere is inert.
        default n
        help
            Pulls the espressif/usb_host_uvc managed component and compiles the
            UVC host and the JPEG decode, so an HDMI grabber plugged into the
            board feeds the Picture service. P4 only: no other chip here has a
            High-Speed USB host, and at Full Speed MJPEG starves. It owns the USB
            host library, so never set it with MM_USB_MIDI_HOST in one image.

    config MM_AUDIO_CODEC
        bool "Audio codecs in front of a microphone (ES8311, ES7210)"
        default y if IDF_TARGET_ESP32P4 || IDF_TARGET_ESP32S31
        default y if (IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3 || IDF_TARGET_ESP32) && !MM_LITE
        default n
        help
            Pulls the esp_codec_dev managed component and compiles the codec
            bring-up, for the boards whose microphone sits behind an ES8311 or
            ES7210, such as the S31 CoreBoard, P4 boards and the Waveshare
            ESP32-S3-RGB-Matrix. On for those chips and the classic ESP32 outside
            the 4 MB tier (MM_LITE); a board with an I2S microphone such as the INMP441 needs no codec.

    config MM_SD_CARD
        bool "microSD card support (SDMMC or SPI)"
        default n if MM_LITE
        default y
        help
            Compiles the FatFs SD card backend, on every chip with an SD host,
            outside the 4 MB tier (MM_LITE).

    config MM_LITE
        bool "The 4 MB tier (-lite firmwares)"
        default n
        help
            Set by sdkconfig.defaults.lite for a firmware that fits a 4 MB board's
            one 2496 KB app slot beside everything else. Every feature that does
            not fit defaults off under it, so the tier is this one symbol. The list
            of what it leaves out, one line per feature added under it, is in
            docs/reference/hardware/firmware-variants.md, "The 4 MB tier".

endmenu
